# What `vercel deploy` from the repository root leaves out of the upload (docs/hosting.md). The
# production deploy is a git push and clones the tree, so this file only matters for CLI previews;
# without it the CLI uploaded the working tree with .turboslide (5 GB of renders) in it.
.git
node_modules
dist
.turboslide
.output
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
.turbo
.tanstack
.nitro
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
*.local
crates/*/target
# Round four (gslides-parity SPEC-4 0.38; the integrator at merge 2): the wasm module under
# packages/native/wasm/ and the Linux x64 glibc addon are committed build products the dither
# worker and the function import, so a CLI preview uploads them the way the git push carries
# them; every other platform's addon stays out (the two lines that excluded the wasm folder
# predate the round, and the preview build of 2026-09-14 failed on the worker's glue import)
*.node
!packages/native/npm/linux-x64-gnu/turboslide-native.linux-x64-gnu.node
.repos
.github
# The WAF rules file is applied through the Vercel API by the integrator, never by the build
# (gslides-parity SPEC-3 8.3, 11.5 R0)
firewall
